---
components: ["CopyText"]
description: Copy text renders a value inline with a compact copy button beside it, for endpoints, IDs, and other single values in a sentence or list.
---

<script>
  import { CopyText, DescriptionList, DescriptionListItem, Text } from "carbon-components-svelte";
</script>

## Basic

Pass the value as the default slot. By default, the button copies the rendered text at click time using the native [Clipboard API](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/Clipboard/writeText), with a `document.execCommand("copy")` fallback when that API is unavailable or rejects. For a standalone icon button, use [CopyButton](/components/CopyButton); for a labeled, editable-looking field, use [CopyInput](/components/CopyInput).

<CopyText>postgres-prod-01.acme.io:5432</CopyText>

## Text

Set `text` to the string to copy. Use it when the copied value differs from what is displayed, such as a truncated URL. When the default slot is empty, `text` is also rendered as the value.

<CopyText text="https://api.acme.io/webhooks/incoming/f8a2c91d">https://api.acme.io/…/f8a2c91d</CopyText>

<CopyText text="f8a2c91d" />

## Inline in text

The value and button flow inline, so `CopyText` sits inside a sentence. Long values wrap, and the button follows the last line. When a value nearly fills its line, the button can drop to the next line by itself.

<Text>Send requests to <CopyText>https://api.acme.io/v1</CopyText> with your API token in the <code>Authorization</code> header.</Text>

## Custom feedback

Set `feedback` to customize the message shown after copying. Set `errorFeedback` to customize the message shown when copying fails (default `"Failed to copy"`). Set `feedbackTimeout` to change how long feedback stays visible, in milliseconds (default `2000`).

<CopyText text="f8a2c91d" feedback="Webhook ID copied" feedbackTimeout={4000} />

## Icon description

Set `iconDescription` to change the button's accessible name and hover tooltip. Give each button a distinct name when several appear on one page, so screen readers can tell them apart.

<CopyText text="postgres-prod-01.acme.io:5432" iconDescription="Copy endpoint" />

## Copy behavior

Pass a function to `copy` to replace the default clipboard behavior. It receives the resolved text. On failure it should reject, so the button shows `errorFeedback` and dispatches `copy:error`. The component dispatches `copy` after a successful copy.

<CopyText text="f8a2c91d" copy={(text) => navigator.clipboard.writeText(text.toUpperCase())} />

## Tooltip

The button shows a portalled tooltip on hover and focus, and the same surface shows the feedback after copying. Set `tooltipPosition` and `tooltipAlignment` to place it; see [CopyButton](/components/CopyButton#hover-tooltip) for the full behavior.

<CopyText text="f8a2c91d" tooltipPosition="right" />

## Description list

Place `CopyText` in a `DescriptionListItem` to make one value copyable. The value is copied as rendered, or set `text` to copy something different from what is displayed.

<DescriptionList>
  <DescriptionListItem term="Name">postgres-prod-01</DescriptionListItem>
  <DescriptionListItem term="Endpoint"><CopyText>postgres-prod-01.acme.io:5432</CopyText></DescriptionListItem>
  <DescriptionListItem term="Webhook"><CopyText text="https://api.acme.io/webhooks/incoming/f8a2c91d">https://api.acme.io/…/f8a2c91d</CopyText></DescriptionListItem>
  <DescriptionListItem term="Region">us-east-1</DescriptionListItem>
</DescriptionList>
